From 288fb0e7a0db784fbcea7f7c1af3a5ebe714d9c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:13:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): hub admission no longer admits
 board_admin_key / instance_role_ssm

The hub-admission-test rubric dropped both needs (state PR #1598, David's option A on
t_01a1cdb45e11f673): hub-admin from a capability:hub-write worker reaches the Board admin key
and the instance role, so they are hub-write work, not hub admission needs.

- NEEDS drops both ids, so a judge reply that still names one fails validation (deny).
- The comment-relay rule's hub-context regex drops their ids and prose (admin key,
  instance role, ssm, board admin credential/token): a relay card naming them now gets the
  relay route instead of a judge call.
- The kanban_create hub_reason description no longer lists them and points at hub-admin.

Proof: tests/test_kanban_hub_admission.py::test_retired_hub_write_needs_are_not_admitted
fails on main (validated() returns an admit Verdict) and passes here; the relay test
test_retired_hub_write_needs_do_not_exempt_a_relay likewise. Route-provenance admit fixture
moved to hub_chrome. 13 hub-admission/relay files: 207 passed.

Card: t_01a1d0b13f7f234d
